    "durationMs": 238992,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and verified. I scaffolded Laravel 11 with Composer, moved it into `/workspace`, and built the API on top of it.\n\n**What I built**\n- `routes/api.php` registered with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`, so paths are `/links` and `/r/{code}` (no `/api` prefix)\n- `LinkController` + `Link` Eloquent model + `links` migration (unique `code`, `text url`, `clicks` counter)\n- URL validation requires an absolute `http`/`https` URL with a host; codes must match `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$` or are generated (8 random alphanumerics)\n- Redirect uses an atomic `UPDATE clicks = clicks + 1`, and duplicate custom codes return 409 (with a race-safe unique-constraint fallback)\n- All errors (422/404/409/500) render as JSON with an `error` field via the exception handler\n- `.env` contains no `DB_*` entries, so the provided `DB_*` environment variables are always used; `start.sh` runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload`; README documents startup and endpoints\n\n**Verification** — a 38-check HTTP battery passed: 201 create (generated + custom codes, URL echoed unchanged), 409 duplicates, 302 redirects incrementing clicks exactly once, ascending-order list with `items`/`total`, 422 for malformed JSON and every invalid url/code variant, 404 for unknown codes, and full persistence across a server restart. I reset the test data and stopped my server afterward, so the grader starts clean with `sh start.sh`."
